description: Conventions for Nuxt pages and Vue components.
globs: apps/pwa/pages/**,apps/pwa/components/**
alwaysApply: false
---

## Page vs Component

- **Pages** (`apps/pwa/pages`) should be route-level containers that compose components.
- **Components** (`apps/pwa/components`) should be reusable and focused.
- If UI is used in more than one page, extract to a component.

## Template Rules

- Keep templates simple; move logic to `<script setup>` and computed properties.
- Avoid complex inline expressions in templates.

## Example

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
const props = defineProps<{ title: string }>()
const subtitle = computed(() => `${props.title} summary`)
</script>

<template>
  <section class="space-y-2">
    <h1 class="text-xl font-semibold">{{ props.title }}</h1>
    <p class="text-muted-foreground">{{ subtitle }}</p>
  </section>
</template>
```
